<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Berkeley (governor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1605">1605</a>–<a href="/years/1677">1677</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Berkeley was an English colonial governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, serving from 1641 to 1652 and again from 1660 to 1677. A royalist, he encouraged diversified agriculture but favoured a small circle of planters. His refusal to wage war on Native Americans on the frontier provoked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bacons-rebellion">Bacon's Rebellion</a> in 1676, which he suppressed with many executions before he was recalled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-berkeley-governor.jpg" alt="William Berkeley (governor)" width="320" height="396" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Painter Hariott L.T. Montague after Sir Peter Lely[1] · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Governor_William_Berkeley_(grayscale).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
